# The Linux list: the check line's commands proven on Linux, one id a line (`share.sh ids` names every
# command's id). Read by share.sh, so the PR check's Linux share (check-linux.yml), the twin's matrix
# (check.yml's `suite` jobs), the macOS share and the rest all split the line by this one file.
# CircleCI's static matrix (.circleci/parts/check-linux.yml) must list the same ids: share.sh fails
# when it differs. An id joins once its suite passes on Linux (.circleci/linux-local.sh reproduces one
# on a Mac); off it: sextant, whose suite needs macOS, and wharf-runs' scripts off its LINUX_OK list.
plugin
regatta
regatta-classes
helloworld
plumb
keel
lighthouse
wharf
aurora
atlas
wharf-runs
helm
